    @McpTool(title = "Get Wicket Spring test plan")
    @McpDescription("Return the existing deterministic Spring WicketTester plan and Java scaffold for a concrete top-level source WebPage, Panel or FormComponentPanel with Wicket-Spring injection intent. Requires host projectPath. Returns envelope schema 1 and springTestPlan schema 1: constructor strategy, suggested Mockito bindings, manual binding TODOs, notes, required test dependency coordinates (availability not checked), existing eligible module test roots and exact scaffold source. Optional dependencyGraph links source injection fields to generated mocks or manual setup. Does not choose production bean/profile bindings, execute tests or Spring, create files, change build/root configuration, open a preview, or change sidebar/clipboard state. A completed plan is not a runnable-test or runtime-validity guarantee: review TODOs, mock stubbing, application setup and constructor arguments before adapting it. Plain Wicket and unsupported subjects return TEST_PLAN_UNAVAILABLE. Uses default markup, shared module/source-set selection, disk refresh, smart/committed reads, project isolation, 30-second deadline, freshness checks and 512-KiB response limit. Reinvoke after edits; errors use versioned JSON codes.")
